+---
+id: task-001-fix-three-order-service-bugs-lower-case-sku-lookup-free-shipping-boundary-line-vat-rounding
+type: task
+title: "Fix three order-service bugs: lower-case SKU lookup, free-shipping boundary, line VAT rounding"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Three reports this week:
+
+1. Giulia (sales desk): a product code typed in lower case (e.g. `lb-220`) is refused as unknown,
+   while the same code in capitals works.
+2. Marco (customer): a basket of exactly €50.00 after discount was still charged €4.90 delivery,
+   though the site promises free shipping from €50.
+3. Accounting: some order lines show one cent less VAT than expected, e.g. a €1.99 item at the
+   standard rate (22%) shows €0.43 instead of €0.44.
+
+## Root causes and fixes
+
+1. `Catalog.find` (`src/catalog.ts`) looked up the map with `sku.trim()` instead of the canonical
+   upper-cased form used as the map's key (`canonicalSku`, applied when a product is added). A
+   lower-case or mixed-case SKU therefore never matched. Fixed `find` to call `canonicalSku(sku)`,
+   matching how SKUs are stored.
+2. `shippingCost` (`src/shipping.ts`) used `goods > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS` to decide free
+   shipping, excluding the boundary itself. The README states shipping is free "when the goods come
+   to €50.00 or more", i.e. the boundary is inclusive. Changed the comparison to `>=`.
+3. `lineVat` (`src/tax.ts`) rounded a line's VAT down (`Math.floor`) instead of half up to the cent,
+   as the README requires for every VAT line. Replaced the ad hoc floor division with the existing
+   `percentOf` helper from `src/money.ts`, which already implements half-up rounding and is used
+   elsewhere (e.g. `shippingVat`).
+
+## Tests
+
+Added one characterization/regression test per bug (red before the fix, green after):
+
+- `test/catalog.test.ts`: looks up and sells a product by its lower-case SKU.
+- `test/orders.test.ts`: an order whose goods total exactly €50.00 ships free.
+- `test/orders.test.ts`: a €1.99 standard-rate line charges €0.44 VAT, not €0.43.
+
+All 17 tests in the suite pass (`npm test`).
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `src/catalog.ts`, `src/shipping.ts`, `src/tax.ts` (fixes)
+- `test/catalog.test.ts`, `test/orders.test.ts` (tests)
